    {
      "id": 39496,
      "nameEs": "Enemy Territory: Quake Wars",
      "originalName": "Enemy Territory: Quake Wars",
      "year": 2007,
      "igdbId": 680,
      "popularity": 28,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "best_version",
          "value": "94177",
          "source": "script",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Enemy Territory: Quake Wars",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Enemy Territory: Quake Wars",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Enemy Territory: Quake Wars is a first-person shooter video game developed by Splash Damage and published by Activision for Microsoft Windows, Linux, Mac OS X, PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360. The prequel to Quake II, Quake Wars is set in the same science fiction universe as Quake II and Quake 4, with a minimal back-story serving as a prequel to Quake II. It is the second multiplayer-focused game in the Quake series after Quake III Arena.\n\nQuake Wars features similar gameplay to Wolfenstein: Enemy Territory, but with the addition of controllable vehicles and aircraft as well as multiple AI deployables, asymmetric teams, much larger maps and the option of computer-controlled bot opponents. Unlike the previous Enemy Territory games, Quake Wars is a commercial release rather than a free download.\n\nEnemy Territory: Quake Wars received mostly positive reviews upon release, although it received some criticism on consoles.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Enemy Territory: Quake Wars es un videojuego de disparos en primera persona desarrollado por Splash Damage y publicado por Activision para Microsoft Windows, Linux, Mac OS X, PlayStation 3 y Xbox 360. Precuela de Quake II, Quake Wars se desarrolla en el mismo universo de ciencia ficción que Quake II y Quake 4, con una trama de fondo mínima que sirve de precuela a Quake II. Es el segundo juego de la serie Quake centrado en el multijugador, después de Quake III Arena.\n\nQuake Wars ofrece una jugabilidad similar a Wolfenstein: Enemy Territory, pero añade vehículos y aeronaves controlables, así como múltiples elementos desplegables controlados por IA, equipos asimétricos, mapas mucho más grandes y la opción de enfrentarse a oponentes bots controlados por el ordenador. A diferencia de los anteriores juegos de Enemy Territory, Quake Wars es un lanzamiento comercial y no una descarga gratuita.\n\nEnemy Territory: Quake Wars recibió en su mayoría críticas positivas al salir, aunque tuvo algunas críticas en las consolas.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
